s":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":46,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I repaired the network by feeding it an estimate of the dead W2 pocket readings, and it now scores 45.2 veh-h on dev, against 214.3 before the fix.\n\n**What I changed and why:** with W2 reading 0, the network almost never chose the EW_left phase under heavy load. The left-turn pockets overflowed, the queued left-turners blocked the straight traffic behind them, and the junction gridlocked. I left the two dead input columns alone and added them onto the columns of working inputs, so the network sees this estimate in their place:\n\nW2 estimate = E2 + 0.6·(t_green − 0.2) − 0.25·(phase is EW_left) + 3·q_W1u\n\n- **E2** is the opposite left-turn pocket, served by the same phase with the same demand.\n- **The timer term** makes an idle junction eventually serve EW_left, so W left-turners the network can't see don't wait until the drain cap.\n- **The EW_left correction** stops the timer from holding EW_left on its own.\n- **The q_W1u term** detects W2 overflowing into the upstream lane.\n\n**Parameters changed:** 368 (308 in W1, 60 in b1).\n\n**Simulator calls:** 7 of 10.\n\n| call | version | dev TTS |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | E2 estimate only | 46.0, with 7 vehicles left at the drain cap |\n| 2 | + timer | 45.7, 1 vehicle left |\n| 3 | + EW_left correction + overflow term (final) | **45.2**, none left |\n| 4 | stronger overflow term | 45.2 |\n| 5 | without the overflow term | 45.5 |\n| 6–7 | + fix for a lone car on lane N1 being ignored (a flaw of the original network) | 45.3 / 45.5, so not used |\n\n**Dev TTS of final weights:** 45.2 (low 34.8, nominal 45.5, high 55.4). The network with every detector working scores 44.5.\n\n**Test predictions:** low 34.9, nominal 45.5, high 56.0.\n\nAll three deliverables are in `work/`.","ttft_ms":1269,"type":"result","duration_ms":930718,"uuid":"a28f6843-ef0a-48ed-a4df-4e83577dd6f1","ttft_stream_ms":1075,"time_to_request_ms":35,"time_to_request_